From: Luiz Irber <luiz@earthmover.io>
Subject: [PATCH] Count points rows through the frame's own filesystem

`SpatialData.__repr__` counts the rows of a points element from the parquet
metadata of its backing files. It opens them as local paths, so the repr of
an object read from any other fsspec filesystem raises `FileNotFoundError`.
A `memory://` path reproduces it.

`get_dask_backing_files` also resolves every parquet path against the working
directory. A path that another filesystem names, such as `bucket/key`, is not
a local path. This resolves only the paths of a local read, which the read
task's `ParquetFunctionWrapper.fs` identifies.

The repr reads the metadata through the frame's own filesystem when it has
one. Two tests cover it: the backing files of a `DirFileSystem` read keep
their paths, and the repr of a `memory://` round trip shows the row counts.

diff --git a/src/spatialdata/_core/spatialdata.py b/src/spatialdata/_core/spatialdata.py
index 2f194e3..ef7bbcc 100644
--- a/src/spatialdata/_core/spatialdata.py
+++ b/src/spatialdata/_core/spatialdata.py
@@ -2080,7 +2080,10 @@ class SpatialData:
                     length: int | None = None
                     backing_files = get_dask_backing_files(v)
                     if backing_files:
-                        length = sum(pq.read_metadata(f).num_rows for f in backing_files)
+                        # Read through the frame's own filesystem: a remote or in-memory parquet
+                        # has no local path.
+                        filesystem = getattr(getattr(v, "expr", None), "filesystem", None)
+                        length = sum(pq.read_metadata(f, filesystem=filesystem).num_rows for f in backing_files)
 
                     n = len(get_axes_names(v))
                     dim_string = f"({n}D points)"
